its origin and its terms. Where terms are uncertain, that is stated rather
than assumed.


REDISTRIBUTED IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------------

satellite.js 4.1.4  —  rebuild/satellite.min.js, archive/rebuild/satellite.min.js
    Copyright (c) 2013 Shashwat Kandadai and UCSC
    MIT License · https://github.com/shashwatak/satellite-js
    Vendored and sha256-pinned (d8a9d17a8a61c8a9237cbd476baa1e31fda3c77aeb4bb014cfebded766af7043)
    so the map and the verifier provably execute the same propagator.
    The upstream licence header is retained verbatim inside the minified file.

Natural Earth II raster tiles  —  tiles/NaturalEarthII/
    Natural Earth raster and vector map data is in the public domain; no
    permission is needed to use it. Attribution is given here as a courtesy
    requested by the project. https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/

CelesTrak GP data  —  archive/pipeline/*.tle, archive/pipeline/satcat_raw.csv,
                      archive/pipeline/omm_*.json, data/india_objects.json
    General Perturbations element sets and the satellite catalogue are
    produced by the 18th Space Defense Squadron, United States Space Force
    (USSPACECOM), and distributed publicly via CelesTrak (https://celestrak.org).
    The underlying element sets are a work of the United States Government.
    These files are redistributed here unmodified because the receipt chain
    commits to the exact bytes as fetched; a verifier cannot check a claim
    against data it does not have.
    Users intending commercial redistribution should consult CelesTrak's
    current terms of use directly rather than relying on this notice.

    Accuracy statement, restated from the source: TLE and OMM data are mean
    elements. They are NOT suitable for conjunction assessment or operational
    collision avoidance.


